---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const guides = [
  ['how-to-compare-unit-prices', 'How to Compare Unit Prices', 'Start with price divided by quantity. Work through weight, volume, and count comparisons, and learn when a small price difference matters.'],
  ['bigger-vs-smaller-package', 'Bigger Package vs. Smaller Package: Is Bigger Really Cheaper?', 'Compare small and large packages, then account for what you can actually use, store, and afford to buy today.'],
  ['multipacks-bogo-multibuy', 'Multipacks, BOGO & Multi-Buy Deals: How to Compare Them', 'Turn bundle prices and buy-one-get-one offers into a total price and total quantity you can compare.'],
  ['sale-price-vs-unit-price', 'Sale Price vs. Unit Price: Which Deal Actually Saves More?', 'Check whether a discount beats another package or brand, with examples of percentage savings, coupons, and checkout costs.'],
  ['mixed-unit-comparisons', 'How to Compare Mixed Units Without Misleading Math', 'Convert ounces and pounds, grams and kilograms, and milliliters and liters—and recognize measurements that should stay separate.'],
  ['when-lowest-unit-price-isnt-enough', 'When the Lowest Unit Price Is Not the Whole Decision', 'Put unit price beside shelf life, storage, cash outlay, promotion restrictions, and your household’s actual usage.'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Shopping Guides for Comparing Deals | Which Deal's Better?" description="Practical guides to unit prices, package sizes, multipacks, BOGO offers, and sale prices, with worked shopping examples.">
  <section class="content-section"><div class="shell">
    <div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Everyday shopping decisions</p><h1>Shopping guides</h1>
    <p>A lower sticker price, a larger box, and a bright sale tag can each point to a different purchase. These guides show how to put the numbers on the same basis, then consider the things a unit price cannot tell you: whether you need the quantity, have room for it, and will use it.</p>
    <p>Start with unit prices if you are comparing different sizes for the first time. If a promotion is the confusing part, choose the guide that matches the offer. All prices in the examples are illustrative, so you can follow the arithmetic without needing a particular store or product.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid guide-grid">{guides.map(([slug, title, description]) => <article class="info-card"><h2><a href={'/guides/' + slug + '/'}>{title}</a></h2><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
    <div class="prose"><h2>Have the package details ready?</h2><p>Use <a href="/">Compare Deals</a> for up to five options, the <a href="/coupon-comparator/">Coupon Comparator</a> for final-price promotions, or browse the <a href="/shopping-examples/">worked examples</a>. Our <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> explains supported units, multipacks, ties, discounts, usage rates, and stock-up estimates.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .guide-grid{margin-top:2rem}
  .guide-grid h2{font-size:1.25rem;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 .75rem}
  @media(min-width:760px){.guide-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
</style>
